def table(rows,widths):
    converted=[[Paragraph(str(c),styles['SmallClean']) for c in row] for row in rows]
    t=Table(converted,colWidths=widths,hAlign='LEFT'); t.setStyle(TableStyle([('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,0),HexColor('#edf1f6')),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'TOP'),('LEFTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),10),('RIGHTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),10),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),10),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),9),('LINEBELOW',(0,0),(-1,0),.6,HexColor('#c7d0dc')),('LINEBELOW',(0,1),(-1,-1),.3,HexColor('#e3e8ee'))]));story.append(t);story.append(Spacer(1,16))
def page(): story.append(PageBreak())
p('PRODUCT AND TECHNICAL BRIEF / 11 OCTOBER 2026','SmallClean')
p('ImpactGuard','TitleClean')
h('Validate business outcomes after code changes')
p('A checkout can return HTTP 200 while fewer customers complete a purchase. A banking service can report success while the bank has not settled a transfer. These failures require business evidence as well as application telemetry.')
p('ImpactGuard is a working prototype for developers and business operators, available locally and as a public Cloud Run demo. It measures outcome changes, inspects candidate commits, separates regression hypotheses from other anomalies, and records a human review decision. It does not modify application code or repair transactions.')
h('Who would pay for it?')
p('An independent Shopify seller needs to know whether a release reduced completed orders or introduced unprofitable discounts. A payment team needs to find ledger credits that lack settlement evidence. The product reduces the work required to assemble an investigation; its value depends on accurate data, useful attribution, and fewer false alerts.')
table([['Product question','Evidence to inspect'],['Did a release reduce checkout completion?','Comparable session windows, payment segments, deployed commit timing, changed redirect logic.'],['Did a discount change make orders unprofitable?','Order amounts, combined discounts, configured costs, changed promotion logic.'],['Are recorded credits backed by settled transfers?','Bank state, application state, immutable postings, exact integer-cent totals.']],[190,322])
p('Public demonstration: impactguard-182850660018.us-central1.run.app. Repository: github.com/vishnusreddy/impactguard. All current demonstration scenarios use explicitly labeled synthetic data.','SmallClean')
page();h('How it differs from existing observability products')
p('New Relic is not limited to runtime exceptions. It supports custom events, business attributes, queries, dashboards, and alerts [1]. Sentry also provides release context and suspect-commit workflows [2]. Business metrics and commit correlation alone are not defensible claims of novelty.')
p('ImpactGuard proposes a narrower workflow: validate a business outcome, examine a candidate code change, inspect the financial implication, and decide whether the finding is a regression or another kind of issue. It can complement an observability platform. The comparison below describes product emphasis, not exclusive capabilities.')
table([['Area','Established tools','ImpactGuard prototype'],['Primary workflow','Broad application and infrastructure observability; configurable custom telemetry.','Business-outcome investigation with commerce and settlement examples.'],['Business measurements','Custom events and metrics can represent purchases and other outcomes [1].','Opinionated completion-rate, margin, cohort, and settlement checks.'],['Code context','Release and suspect-commit features already exist in products such as Sentry [2].','Read-only, multiple-repository import; bounded diff inspection and Gemini candidate attribution.'],['Financial validation','Can be implemented using custom data and queries.','Exact-cent settlement checks and disclosed revenue-exposure formulas.'],['AI','Do not assume competing products lack AI.','Vertex anomaly detection, classification, and code-line investigation. Configured locally with personal Vertex AI.'],['Decision and action','Capabilities vary by product and configuration.','Manual resolve, ignore, not-an-issue, and reopen. No automatic repair.']],[100,200,212])
p('The business hypothesis is faster investigation for a small team without a dedicated observability engineer. This remains to be tested with real customers; the prototype does not establish commercial superiority.','SmallClean')
page();h('Seller example: Luma Goods')
p('Luma Goods sells through its own Shopify storefront. The demonstration assumes 120 checkout starts per day and an $82 average order value. These inputs are assumptions, not collected seller revenue.')
p('After a synthetic checkout release, completion declines for Safari sessions using PayPal while other segments remain near baseline. ImpactGuard shows the affected segment, sample sizes, a candidate redirect-handling diff, and estimated daily exposure. The temporal association is a hypothesis, not proof of causation.')
h('Investigation sequence')
table([['Step','Operator workflow'],['1. Collect','In Integrations, select a sample case and collect Shopify and GA4 data. Generated data is clearly labeled. Real connectors remain disconnected.'],['2. Measure','Compare baseline and recent outcome rates. Validate collection completeness and traffic mix before assigning a cause.'],['3. Inspect code','Connect frontend, checkout, and backend repositories under one project. Inspect bounded commit diffs. Supply deployment mapping before attributing a live issue.'],['4. Analyze','Request Vertex analysis when personal credentials are configured. The model decides whether the window contains an issue, classifies it, and investigates candidate code.'],['5. Review','Mark resolved, ignore, mark not an issue, or reopen. Review state changes preserve source measurements and ledger evidence.']],[90,422])
p('Revenue exposure = (baseline completion rate - current completion rate) x daily checkout starts x average order value. This is a projection under an unchanged-volume assumption, not realized loss or recovered revenue.')
p('The source collector and the synthetic dashboard are separate. The current version does not join Shopify customers to GA4 users, schedule ingestion, or prove that an imported commit was deployed. Those production capabilities require explicit data definitions and deployment events.','SmallClean')
page();h('Banking validation and issue classification')
p('The banking fixture contains 2,000 transfers. In 200 cases, the application marks success while the bank reports failed or pending. The fixture contains $46,998.09 in credits without confirmed settlement. Exact integer-cent arithmetic computes the mismatch; a language model does not calculate the ledger balance.')
p('The investigation points to a candidate status-mapping change that treats most non-cancelled statuses as success. An operator can review the evidence and mark the finding resolved, but that action does not reverse credits, alter transaction statuses, or assert that settlement has occurred.')
table([['Classification','Meaning and evidence requirement'],['Business regression','An outcome change with release and changed-behavior evidence. Candidate causation still requires verification.'],['Traffic anomaly','Traffic volume or mix changed. A spike alone does not establish a code regression.'],['Security signal','Possible attack indicators, such as elevated blocked requests. This does not establish a confirmed compromise.'],['Operational incident','Service, fulfillment, or process behavior changed without sufficient code-regression evidence.'],['Data quality','Missing, delayed, duplicated, or inconsistent measurements can explain the apparent change.'],['Inconclusive','Insufficient evidence or missing deployed-commit mapping. Do not force a regression verdict.']],[130,382])
p('Sample cases include a checkout decline, a traffic spike, possible attack signals, and a purchase-event collection gap. The delivery fixture is assessed by Gemini; the current cached decision is healthy. It is not assigned a preset incident category. Security signals must remain separate from regressions.','SmallClean')
page();h('Where AI is used')
p('AI should interpret evidence and help investigate causes. Numerical validation must remain reproducible. Increasing the number of model calls does not increase reliability; the product uses AI where semantic judgment adds value.')
table([['Stage','Implementation','Current activation'],['Business measurement','SQL aggregates, comparable-window rates, exact-cent ledger checks.','Deterministic; available locally.'],['Synthetic scenario screening','SQL supplies measurements; Gemini decides whether an issue is present.','LLM decision; unassessed when AI is unavailable.'],['Source anomaly classification','Vertex reads aggregate evidence and configurable checks; returns a typed issue category.','Enabled and verified locally with Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite.'],['Cause investigation','Gemini selects a commit, file, and new diff line; explains the defect and rules out alternatives.','Enabled and verified locally with Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite.'],['Candidate commit ranking','Gemini compares all bounded eligible diffs. References are checked against supplied code.','LLM attribution; deployment mapping required.'],['Fix and guard drafts','Gemini suggests a fix diff and a guard-test diff. Neither is applied or executed.','Human review only.']],[125,242,145])
h('Cost controls')
p('Analysis runs on an operator request, not on dashboard polling or every event. Requests contain compact aggregate evidence rather than raw customers. Input is bounded; detection output is limited to 1,000 tokens and attribution to 2,600. Identical requests are cached in memory. The default budget is 20 model attempts per server process. Invalid model output is rejected without changing evidence.')
p('Live AI is verified in a dedicated personal project. A checkout investigation used 1,163 input tokens and 106 output tokens; the repeated request returned from the local cache. At the current global standard rates of $0.30 per million input tokens and $2.50 per million output tokens, this request is approximately $0.0006, excluding taxes and other services [5]. This is an estimate, not a billing invoice.','SmallClean')
p('No Vertex request used the work account. The application loads only explicitly selected personal credentials. When configuration is absent, the interface reports an unassessed window, with no rule-based verdict fallback.','SmallClean')
page();h('Measured attribution evaluation')
p('Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite selected the planted commit and a validated file/line in 25 of 25 cases. The previous keyword/timing heuristic selected the target in 1 of 25. All cases remained in the denominator; there were no validation errors. Detection and attribution used 78,858 total tokens across 50 requests.')
table([['Measure','Gemini','Keyword baseline'],['Top-1 candidate commit','25 / 25','1 / 25'],['Valid target file and new line','25 / 25','Not produced'],['Invalid responses / errors','0 / 25','Not applicable']],[230,141,141])
p('Each controlled business-contract fixture has five eligible commits, including a keyword-heavy logging decoy. The old code passes the contract and the planted new code violates it. Cases cover settlement, idempotency, refunds, discounts, checkout, delivery, and rounding.')
p('This is development-set evidence from a small synthetic stress test, not a held-out study or production accuracy. Deliberate keyword decoys disadvantage the keyword baseline. A first diagnostic run used inconsistent before-code; that run is retained in the repository and excluded from the corrected v2 benchmark. The reported result does not prove causation or establish false-positive rates.')
p('A separate six-case detector check returned the expected verdict/category for stable metrics, planned traffic growth, reconciled ledger entries, unexplained traffic spikes, credential-stuffing signals, and missing purchase events. Six of six passed. This small check does not estimate production false-positive rates.')
h('Banking account review')
p('Gemini reviews grouped mismatch evidence and flags accounts with repeated failed or pending transfers recorded as successful credits. Flags cite account IDs and transaction IDs. They request review; they do not establish exploitation, accuse users, or block accounts.')
h('Closing demonstration')
p('Open an investigation, inspect the highlighted candidate line and ruled-out commits, then review the suggested fix and guard-test diffs. Both drafts remain unapplied and unexecuted. An operator can resolve, ignore, or mark the finding not an issue; those decisions do not alter financial records.')
page();h('Integrations, security, and deployment readiness')
p('One project can connect up to 10 GitHub repositories. Import fetches recent commit metadata and bounded patches, filters sensitive filenames, and redacts known credential patterns before storage. Public repositories need no token; private import uses an explicit read-only token. The application does not read ambient GitHub CLI authentication.')
p('Shopify collection uses the Admin GraphQL API [3], a configured store domain, and a dedicated token. It reads up to 500 recent orders without requesting customer or card details. GA4 collection uses the Data API [4] with a dedicated credential file and read-only scope; it requests daily sessions, purchases, and revenue. Live account collection has not been validated with user accounts.')
h('Credential boundaries')
p('Credentials remain in local environment variables or dedicated files excluded from Git. They are not included in AI prompts, application API responses, or provider-error logs. Provider authentication necessarily sends credentials only to the intended provider. Pattern redaction is defense in depth; it cannot identify every possible secret format. Keep secrets out of repositories and analysis instructions.')
h('Personal Vertex setup')
p('Configure IMPACTGUARD_VERTEX_PROJECT, IMPACTGUARD_VERTEX_CREDENTIALS, and GEMINI_MODEL. The adapter loads only the explicitly selected credential file. It does not use ambient gcloud credentials or the existing work project. Install optional Python dependencies before enabling live analysis.')
h('Readiness and next steps')
p('The app is deployed on scale-to-zero Cloud Run with durable Cloud Storage checkpoints. The public preview uses isolated synthetic data and cached Gemini investigations. Owner access protects account connections, private data, review changes, and new paid AI requests. It is not a multi-user production service. Before production, add authentication, managed secrets, scheduled collection, consistent metric definitions, release-to-repository mappings, source freshness checks, retention controls, and integration tests against selected accounts.')
p('Recommended pilot: one seller, one checkout journey, known releases, and daily comparison against order records. Evaluate false-positive rate, investigation time, and whether candidate causes are useful. Do not claim prevented losses from manual review decisions.')
page();h('Demonstration guide and references')
p('Open Integrations and collect both samples. Analyze the checkout decline: without release mapping it remains inconclusive. Select Traffic spike and collect again; analyze to show a traffic anomaly. Select Possible attack signals to show a security signal, then the collection gap to show data quality. These examples demonstrate classification boundaries without account access.')
p('Open Codebases to attach multiple repositories. Explain that a connected repository is not proof of deployment. Run the checkout or banking demo scenario, open its investigation, inspect the AI-highlighted candidate line and unapplied fix/test drafts, and mark the issue ignored or resolved. Show that the source metrics and ledger mismatches remain unchanged.')
p('For an AI demonstration, configure a personal Vertex project and explicit credentials, then select Analyze metrics or Run analysis. Show the provider, classification, verification step, and cache behavior. If credentials are absent, present the feature as implemented but unconnected.')
h('Primary references')
